{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Who sits upon the vault (חוג).</b> From the same root as ובמחוגה (Isaiah 44:13). The meaning: the instrument that makes the circle, which is the line surrounding in a circle. Now, it is established that the earth is round, not square — though there is no need for this verse, for the matter is known by absolute proofs. And the meaning of 'who sits' is that all is filled with His glory:" "<b>Like a curtain (כדק).</b> Like כשפריר (Jeremiah 43:10), and it resembles the form of a tent. And these 'heavens' are not the spheres:" "<b>And spreads them out (וימתחם).</b> Like ויפרשם ('and spreads them out'):" "<b>To dwell (לשבת).</b> Beneath Him. And the meaning is that HaShem is the one who sits upon the vault of the earth:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {1 "Resolved the lemma as כדק (for the standard כדוק, 'like a daq'), following the Hebrew as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:15.217974400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}